  <!-- Client Libraries -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="section-title" id="client-libraries">Client Libraries</h2>
      <p class="doc-text">
        Town OS ships with Go and JavaScript client libraries that provide full API coverage.
        Both clients throw typed errors on non-200 responses using
        <a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9457" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RFC 9457</a>
        problem detail.
      </p>

      <h3 id="go-client">Go Client</h3>
      <p class="doc-text">
        The Go client lives in <code>src/svc/systemcontroller/client.go</code> and implements
        the <code>Client</code> interface. It supports both Unix socket and HTTP connections.
      </p>
      <pre><code>// Connect via Unix domain socket (production)
client := systemcontroller.InitClient("/run/town-os/systemcontroller.sock")

// Connect via HTTP (development / testing)
client := systemcontroller.FromClient(http.DefaultClient, "http://localhost:5309")</code></pre>
      <p class="doc-text">
        Set <code>client.Token</code> after authenticating. All methods accept a
        <code>context.Context</code> as their first parameter.
      </p>

